his way around federal infrastructure policy. But Leanne and Jose were nowhere near the millions of dollars they needed for the local contribution to the cost. They needed help. And in the year 2000, help arrived in the unlikely form of an ecologist. So how does a community of 2,000 people that's severely economically disadvantaged come up with millions of dollars? They're not going to do that selling tamales. This is Ryan Lustor from The Nature Conservancy. And he would end up being a key part of the solution
联邦基础设施政策的律师。但莉安和何塞距离支付本地分摊费用所需的数百万美元还差得远。他们需要帮助。2000年，救星以一位生态学家的意想不到的形式出现了。那么，一个严重处于经济劣势的2,000人社区怎么能筹集到数百万美元呢？他们靠卖玉米粉蒸肉是做不到这一点的。这是来自大自然保护协会的瑞安·拉斯特。他最终成为了解决汉密尔顿城面临的

