00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:41.000
This region doesn't get a lot of rain, but the wetlands were irrigated naturally by the rivers that meandered across the valley floor. During winter storms and the spring snowmelt, the Sacramento and the San Joaquin would fan out across the landscape. Occasionally, during really big floods, the entire central valley was transformed into a vast inland sea. It turned the valley into a giant lake, essentially. But in the 19th and 20th century, farmers took over the valley and settled in little towns like Hamilton City. And for them, these erratic seasonal floods
这个地区雨水不多，但湿地得到了蜿蜒穿过谷底的河流的自然灌溉。在冬季风暴和春季融雪期间，萨克拉门托河和圣华金河会在整个景观中扇形散开。偶尔，在真正的大洪水期间，整个中央谷地会变成一片巨大的内陆海。它基本上把山谷变成了一个巨大的湖泊。但在19和20世纪，农民接管了山谷，并在汉密尔顿城这样的小镇定居下来。对他们来说，这些不规律的季节性洪水

