effectively cutting off the wetlands from their water source. Today, the valley is mostly dry, dusty farmland. The marshes and the forests are almost entirely gone. We've lost 95% of this ecosystem up and down the state in the last hundred years, so it's – a lot of people don't know about it or understand it. Levees enabled much of the 20th century development in the Central Valley. But that came at an enormous ecological cost. And it also hasn't guaranteed safety
实际上切断了湿地与其水源的联系。今天，该山谷大部分是干燥、尘土飞扬的农田。沼泽和森林几乎完全消失了。在过去的一百年里，我们在全州范围内失去了95%的这种生态系统，所以很多人并不知道它或不理解它。堤防促进了中央谷地20世纪的大部分开发。但这付出了巨大的生态代价。它也没有保证安全，

