I mean, you're using nature and in this sense, the floodplain, the floodplain is what we're using. It's a storage facility, plain and simple. They drew up a plan for this new setback levee. And as part of the proposal, the Nature Conservancy agreed to buy the 1,400 acres of farmland between the river and the new levy and donate it to the project. That land value would count as Hamilton City's local contribution to the cost of the project.
我的意思是，你在利用自然，在这个意义上，洪泛区，洪泛区就是我们所利用的。它是一个蓄水设施，就这么简单。他们为这个新的退堤计划绘制了蓝图。作为提案的一部分，大自然保护协会同意购买河与新堤防之间的1,400英亩农田，并将其捐赠给该项目。这块土地的价值将被算作汉密尔顿城对项目成本的本地配套投入。

52
00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:33.000
Then, Ryan and his colleagues would do all of the landscape design work to transform that floodplain into the kind of rich ecosystem that might have been there hundreds of years ago. In 2004, the team got the Army Corps of Engineers to do a feasibility study of their new Setback Levy Plan, and they said, hey, this time it's different. This time you have to consider all of these habitat benefits when you calculate the benefit-cost ratio. The Army Corps ran the numbers. And when you added that dollar value of the habitat
然后，瑞安和他的同事们将完成所有的景观设计工作，将该洪泛区改造成几百年前可能存在的丰富生态系统。2004年，该团队让陆军工程兵团对他们的新退堤计划进行了可行性研究，他们说，嘿，这次不同了。这次你们在计算效益成本比时必须考虑所有这些生境效益。陆军工程兵团计算了数字。当你把生境的美元价值

