Story over, Hamilton City gets the protection it deserves. But not so fast. Because it turns out that even if the Army Corps of Engineers approves a plan, that doesn't mean it has the money to actually go through with it. And to get the federal government to pay for its portion of a levy, you have to go convince them. And I don't mean send a really compelling email.
故事结束，汉密尔顿城获得了应有的保护。但别急。因为事实证明，即使陆军工程兵团批准了一项计划，也并不意味着它有钱真正去执行。要让联邦政府为其部分的堤防买单，你必须去说服他们。我的意思不是发一封极具说服力的电子邮件。

